{title: 162 - Wondrous Love}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #162 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Dm}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 162}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]What [C]wondrous love is [Am]this,
[G]O [C]my [Dm]soul, O my [Am]soul?
What wondrous [G]love is [Am]this, [G]O [C]my [Dm]sou[Em]l?[Dm]
[C]What [F]wondrous [Am7]love is [Dm]this
[Bb]That [Am7]caused the [Dm]Lord [C]of [Dm]bli[G]ss
[Dm]To [Em7][Dm]bear the [C]dreadful [Am]cur[Dm]se [C]for my [Dm]soul, [Am]for my [Em]soul;
[Am]To bear the [Bm7]dreadful [Am]curse [C]for [Em]my [Dm]sou[Em]l?[Dm]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]To God and [C]to the Lamb [Am]I will sing,
[G]I will [C]sing; To [Dm]God and [Am]to the Lamb,
[G]I [Am]will [G]sing; [C]To God [Dm]and [Em]to [Dm]the Lamb
[C]Who is [F]the great I [Am7]am, While millions [Dm]join the theme,
[Bb]I will [Am7]sing, I [Dm]will sing; While [C]millions join [Dm]the theme, [G]I will sing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm]And when from death [C]I'm free, I'll sing [Am]on, I'll sing on;
[G]And when [C]from death [Dm]I'm free, [Am]I'll sing on;
[G][Am]And [G]when [C]from [Dm]death [Em]I'm [Dm]free,
[C]I'll sing [F]and joyful [Am7]be, And [Dm]through eternity
[Bb]I'll sing [Am7]on, I'll [Dm]sing on! [C]And through [Dm]eternity, I'll [G]sing on
{end_of_verse}
